AI Secure Controls Framework: how to continue the Subdomain and AI Use Case mapping

What changed

The framework is updated as a working draft. Extra details are removed for now to keep it focused.
Two new columns are added:
Subdomain (column F): the subdomain from Rashi's domain/subdomain structure.
AI use case (column H): which of the 5 AI use case categories the requirement applies to.

Workflow (repeat for each domain)

Step 1. Filter by domain.
Filter the Domain column to one domain at a time (e.g., Data Security, which has 23 of 174 records). Working one domain at a time keeps the subdomain list short and the mapping consistent.

Step 2. Map subdomains with the prompt.
Copy the filtered rows (Requirement ID, Requirement Name, Requirement Description) and the subdomains for that domain from Rashi's document into Prompt 1 below.

Step 3. Verify the subdomain mapping. This is mandatory.
The AI output is only a first pass. Check every row against the requirement description and Rashi's subdomain definitions. Fix anything that doesn't fit, then fill in the Subdomain column. Note any requirement that fits no subdomain; don't force it into one.

Step 4. Map AI use cases with the prompt.
With the same filtered rows, run Prompt 2. The mapping is based on the Requirement Description, not only the name.

Step 5. Verify the use case mapping and fill in the column.
Check the results, especially rows tagged "All". Use the category names exactly as written below so the column stays filterable.

Step 6. Mark the domain as done and move on to the next one.

Conventions

Do not edit requirement text or IDs during this pass.
Multiple use cases: separate with "; " (e.g., Agentic AI; Generative AI). Use All only when the requirement truly applies to all 5.
Ambiguous rows: add a comment in the cell and leave them for group review.

AI use case categories (working definitions, pending client sign-off)

Productivity AI: vendor-hosted AI assistants for employees (M365 Copilot, Amazon Quick). TMCC configures access and data connections but does not build the AI.
Developer AI: AI coding tools in the SDLC (GitHub Copilot, Amazon Kiro, Claude Code).
Vendor Integrated AI: AI embedded in third-party SaaS. TMCC does not control the model. Catch-all for other vendor AI.
Agentic AI: AI that autonomously takes actions via tools and APIs (Copilot Studio agents, MCP).
Generative AI: custom AI apps TMCC builds on its own platform (AWS Bedrock via the AI gateway).

Prompt 1: Subdomain mapping

Map each AI security requirement below to ONE subdomain from the approved list for the domain "[DOMAIN NAME]".

Rules:
- Use only subdomains from the list. Do not invent new ones.
- Judge by the requirement description, not just the name.
- If a requirement fits two subdomains, pick the best fit and note the second.
- If nothing fits, mark "No fit" and explain in one line.
- If unsure, mark "Review".

