Prompt 2: AI use case mapping

Map each AI security requirement below to the AI use case categories it applies to. This is for TMCC, a regulated US financial services company.

Categories:
1. Productivity AI - vendor-hosted AI assistants for employees (M365 Copilot, Amazon Quick); TMCC does not build the AI.
2. Developer AI - AI coding tools in the SDLC (GitHub Copilot, Amazon Kiro, Claude Code).
3. Vendor Integrated AI - AI embedded in third-party SaaS; TMCC does not control the model.
4. Agentic AI - AI that autonomously takes actions via tools/APIs (Copilot Studio agents, MCP).
5. Generative AI - custom AI apps TMCC builds on AWS Bedrock via its AI gateway.

Rules:
- Base the mapping on the requirement description.
- Tag a category only if TMCC can actually implement or verify the requirement for it. E.g., model hosting or guardrail configuration does not apply to Vendor Integrated AI; the equivalent there is a vendor/contract control.
- Governance requirements (policy, inventory, intake, roles, training) usually apply to "All".
- Use "All" only if the requirement truly applies to all 5 categories.
- Separate multiple categories with "; ".
- If unsure, mark "Review".

